in @reality/algebra
in @bauchladen
in @autopoietic
in @fate
in @glue
in @uuid/spectral

# @reality/algebra/silicon — the hardware-altitude species under @reality.
# The species where matter IS the physical substrate the algebra runs on.
#
# A prism that imports `in @reality/algebra/silicon` declares its content
# IS one silicon-altitude orbit under the substrate's gauge action — a
# transistor-state configuration with its executable-algebra reading, a
# LAPACK routine invocation with its numerical semantics, a memory
# topology with its cache-hierarchy behaviour, an ISA + microarchitecture
# pair with its performance envelope, a Fortran-compiled kernel with
# its FFI-linkable signature — each ONE gauge-orbit observed through
# matter-aspect (transistor state) or information-aspect (executable
# algebra) projection.
#
# Homage: Alan Turing (universal computation, 1936); John von Neumann
# (stored-program architecture, 1945; the merger of instructions and
# data as one carrier the substrate here formalizes as one gauge-
# orbit); Margaret Hamilton (Apollo Guidance Computer priority
# discipline, 1969; the hardware-realtime-scheduling ancestor per
# MEMORY [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]]); Cleve Moler (LINPACK
# 1979 → MATLAB 1984 → the LAPACK numerical-algebra lineage that IS
# the substrate's first math↔silicon empirical discharge path); James
# Demmel + Jack Dongarra (LAPACK 1992; the reference numerical-algebra
# library the substrate composes against via @glue/math_silicon).
# The substrate's silicon species inherits from the numerical-computing
# canon; it does NOT invent hardware algebra, it crystallizes the
# routines the canon has been producing as content-addressed objects
# at the silicon altitude.
#
# === The recognition (family-root forward-promise closure) ===
#
# Per `shards/reality.mirror` §3.2.1 (family-root at `253189a7`) and
# per `docs/specs/reality.md` §3.2.1 (canonical) and per `docs/specs/
# silicon.md` (canonical at `27e9067`, the deep substrate-decl for
# @silicon-as-@autopoietic-species): this shard is the hardware-altitude
# sibling species under `@reality/algebra/*`, alongside math, nl,
# code, physics, spectral. The silicon species is the sibling that
# names the hardware-tuned executable-algebra realizations of math-
# altitude content — the target altitude of @glue/math_silicon's
# Mesland correspondence (per `docs/specs/reality-algebra-math-and-
# glue.md` §2.1: the LAPACK case; #74 Standard Model spectral action
# via Chamseddine-Connes operationalizes here).
#
# Status: candidate. This shard closes the family-root §3.2.1 forward-
# promise and lifts the existing @silicon substrate-decl (at
# `27e9067`) into the sibling-species pattern the species-root
# established at `3c7f2b44`. Recognition #106 (family-root gauge-
# collapse) and #108 (math species) precede; this shard is the
# sibling landing on the same species-root as math.
#
# === Connes A side: A acts on H_silicon; the matter and information
#     carriers are the same gauge-orbit under path-c uniformity ===
#
# Per `reality/algebra.mirror` § species pattern and per
# `reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md` §1.2 (adapted to silicon altitude):
# under gauge-collapse semantics (path-c uniformity per `reality.md`
# §2.3), matter_carrier and information_carrier are the SAME TYPE at
# silicon altitude — two nominal labels on the same H_silicon state.
#
# At `@reality/algebra/silicon`, the A-side reading is: A IS the
# substrate's 5-op algebra acting on H_silicon; the silicon species is
# the altitude at which A's action lands as executable operations on
# transistor states (matter aspect) equivalently readable as invocations
# of a compiled algebra-of-silicon (information aspect). The gauge
# action is a homomorphism A → End(H_silicon) whose image lives in the
# algebra of endomorphisms of the silicon-altitude Hilbert space.
#
# Unlike the math species (where A IS the content per §1.2 of
# `reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md`), the silicon species carries A
# as gauge that acts UPON the silicon-altitude carriers. This is the
# NON-reflexive counterpart: math is the highest-reflexive species
# (A is content); silicon is the highest-hardware-embodied species
# (A executes on transistors). The two compose via @glue/math_silicon
# per §3.3.1 of `reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md`.
#
# === What gets crystallized ===
#
# The Bauchladen of `@reality/algebra/silicon` accumulates content-
# addressed crystals at the silicon altitude. The crystal kinds are
# not exhaustive but the substrate already pulls toward the following
# per `silicon.md` §1.2's apply-discipline enumeration:
#
#   - **Fortran-compiled numerical routines.** Matter aspect: the
#     compiled binary + its ISA-specific instruction stream. Information
#     aspect: the numerical semantics (the linear-algebra operation
#     the routine computes). Forward-promised first crystal: LAPACK
#     `dpotrf` + `dpotrs` (the Cholesky decomposition + triangular-
#     solve pair) per the Q4 forward-promise at `docs/specs/cascade-
#     ffi-runtime-link.md` §7 and per Reed's dpotrf binding work.
#
#   - **LAPACK / BLAS invocations.** Matter aspect: the FFI call site
#     + argument-marshalling shape (column-major layout, leading
#     dimensions, work-space allocation). Information aspect: the
#     linear-algebra semantics (matrix solve, eigendecomposition, SVD,
#     factorization). Existing operational hint: `bootstrap/src/
#     sheaf_laplacian.rs::lambda_zero` calling `prismqueer::ffi::
#     eigenvalues` → LAPACK `dsyev`.
#
#   - **Kernel-call crystals.** Matter aspect: the kernel invocation
#     shape (batch size, tile shape, SIMD width, cache-blocking factor).
#     Information aspect: the algebraic operation the kernel realizes.
#     Forward-promised at the @glue/math_silicon Mesland-correspondence
#     landing.
#
#   - **ISA + microarch signatures.** Matter aspect: the (ISA family,
#     extensions vector, vendor, pointer-width) tuple from
#     `@epistemologic/reality/silicon/arch`. Information aspect: the
#     SIMD dispatch policy that follows (NEON vs SVE vs AVX-512 vs
#     AMX). Content-addressed as prior-art at @fate consultations for
#     routine selection.
#
#   - **Memory-topology crystals.** Matter aspect: the (memory model,
#     total bytes, page size, cache hierarchy, NUMA topology) tuple
#     from `@epistemologic/reality/silicon/memory`. Information aspect:
#     the UMA-aware vs explicit-DMA vs NUMA-migration codegen policy
#     that follows. Content-addressed as prior-art at codegen boundaries.
#
#   - **Compute-budget crystals.** Matter aspect: the (cores, RAM,
#     GPU RAM, wall-clock, spectral-reduction) budget tuple from
#     `@epistemologic/reality/silicon/compute_bound`. Information
#     aspect: the tournament-restriction policy @fate applies when
#     selecting a routine.
#
#   - **Flake-reference crystals.** Matter aspect: the (URL, locked
#     OID, sub-flake path) reference from `@epistemologic/reality/
#     silicon/flake_ref`. Information aspect: the reproducible-build
#     handle the user controls; the substrate's link into the Nix
#     dependency graph.
#
# The crystallization is content-addressed. Each crystal is identified
# by the Blake3 OID of its typed-structure fields plus its
# (matter_carrier, information_carrier) projection labels. The
# crystals accumulate monotonically in the silicon Bauchladen; later
# @fate consultations at the silicon altitude (or at silicon↔X via
# @glue) load these crystals as prior-art inputs. Per `silicon.md`
# §1.3 negative #3: this is content-addressed pre-compiled algebra,
# not JIT compilation. The compilation happened at crystallization
# time; the selection happens at use time.
#
# === @io discharge surfaces ===
#
# The silicon species' @io discharge surfaces are the hardware-facing
# link boundaries already operational in the wider systems-programming
# canon. Per `reality.md` §3.2.1 and per `silicon.md` §1.3 negative
# #5: @silicon does NOT bypass @io; it feeds @io with hardware-tuned
# routines.
#
# Forward-promised discharge surfaces:
#
#   - **@io/silicon (cargo subprocess semantics)** — the cargo/rustc
#     invocation shape the substrate uses to compile crystals into
#     linkable artifacts. Discharge via a typed projection.
#
#   - **@io/silicon (LLVM IR lowering)** — the LLVM-IR emission path
#     for content that lowers below the substrate-decl altitude.
#     Discharge via a `splinter(ast)`-typed projection (per MEMORY
#     [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]) into @facet/llvm.
#
#   - **@io/silicon (LAPACK column-major FFI)** — the FFI ABI the
#     substrate uses to invoke Fortran-compiled numerical routines.
#     The Q4 case; Reed's dpotrf binding operationalizes here.
#
#   - **@io/silicon (dynamic-library link)** — the runtime `.dylib` /
#     `.so` link path for content that binds against host libraries
#     (OpenBLAS, Accelerate, MKL, Apple vecLib per `silicon.md` §1.2).
#
#   - **@io/silicon (Nix flake reference)** — the reproducible-build
#     link via the flake_ref carrier; the substrate's handshake with
#     the Nix dependency graph.
#
# The substrate does NOT commit to ONE discharge surface; the species
# shard declares the discharge surfaces as an OPEN enumeration. @fate's
# tournament selects which discharge to use per emission based on the
# receiver's @io context (LAPACK FFI for a numerical-routine call;
# LLVM IR for a low-level codegen; cargo subprocess for a whole-
# workspace build; flake_ref for a reproducible-build spec).
#
# Each discharge is mediated by @glass's
# `imperfect<discharge_outcome, silicon_surface, transparency(
# discharge)>` carrier; residual opacity (precision loss on numerical
# routines, ABI mismatches, runtime-link failures, NUMA-migration
# overhead) is surfaced via the transparency slot.
#
# === Composition with siblings via @glue (forward-promised) ===
#
# Per `reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md` §2 the silicon species
# composes with the other five siblings via per-pair @glue species.
# The math↔silicon pair is load-bearing (the Cholesky arc's first
# empirical crystal); the other pairs are forward-promised.
#
#   `@glue/math_silicon`   math ↔ silicon (LAPACK case; Cholesky
#                          first empirical crystal; #74 Standard
#                          Model spectral action via Chamseddine-
#                          Connes operationalizes here).
#   `@glue/nl_silicon`     nl ↔ silicon (Reed's shell + config lang
#                          territory; forward-promised).
#   `@glue/code_silicon`   code ↔ silicon (the compilation boundary;
#                          cargo/rustc/llvm invocation; forward-
#                          promised; existing @cascade family carries
#                          the code-source side).
#   `@glue/physics_silicon` physics ↔ silicon (numerical simulation
#                          of physical field configurations; cosmos-
#                          mirror's discharge boundary at silicon
#                          altitude; forward-promised).
#   `@glue/spectral_silicon` spectral ↔ silicon (substrate-on-substrate
#                          at hardware altitude; the substrate reasoning
#                          about its own hardware realizations;
#                          forward-promised).
#
# Per Taut Pass-2 discipline: the future `@glue/<sibling>_silicon` and
# `@glue/silicon_<sibling>` shards MUST inherit `in @glue` and MUST
# NOT re-declare Tomm probes; the morphism family lives at @glue.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Universal computation    Turing 1936 ("On computable numbers",
#                            Proc. London Math. Soc. 42); the
#                            foundational grounding of what silicon
#                            realizes.
#   Stored-program           von Neumann 1945 (First Draft of a Report
#                            on the EDVAC); the merger of instructions
#                            and data as one addressable carrier the
#                            silicon species formalizes as one gauge-
#                            orbit.
#   Realtime scheduling      Hamilton 1969 (Apollo Guidance Computer);
#                            hard+soft realtime priority discipline
#                            per MEMORY [[architecture-hamilton-
#                            scheduler]].
#   Numerical algebra        Moler 1979 (LINPACK); Dongarra-Demmel-
#                            et al. 1992 (LAPACK); the reference
#                            numerical-algebra library the substrate
#                            composes against.
#   Cache-oblivious algs     Frigo-Leiserson-Prokop-Ramachandran 1999
#                            (FOCS); the discipline that makes silicon-
#                            altitude crystals portable across cache
#                            hierarchies.
#   Roofline model           Williams-Waterman-Patterson 2009 (CACM);
#                            the compute-vs-memory-bandwidth
#                            characterization silicon crystals sit
#                            within.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/silicon.md (canonical at `27e9067`, the
#               deep substrate-decl for @silicon-as-@autopoietic-species
#               that `@reality/algebra/silicon` composes with; §1.1
#               the family-root prism class; §1.2 the substrate's
#               apply-discipline enumeration of what already exists;
#               §1.3 five structural negatives);
#               docs/specs/reality.md §3.2.1 (the family-root forward-
#               promise this shard closes); §2.5 (the four invariances
#               each species discharges);
#               docs/specs/reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md §2.1 (the
#               math↔silicon Mesland correspondence; the LAPACK case);
#               §5.3 (the math↔silicon first empirical crystal via
#               LAPACKPrism);
#               docs/specs/cascade-ffi-runtime-link.md §7 (the Q4
#               LAPACK FFI case).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-connes-spectral-triple]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]],
#                      [[architecture-mirror-as-expanding-hilbert-space]] (#51),
#                      [[architecture-flang-mirror-numerical-split]]
#                       (the D→flang dispatch discipline the silicon
#                        species terminates at the numerical altitude),
#                      [[architecture-hamilton-scheduler]]
#                       (the hardware-realtime scheduling discipline
#                        the silicon species inherits at the runtime
#                        boundary),
#                      [[architecture-fate-is-optical-inference]] (#58)
#                       (@fate's tournament selection at silicon altitude
#                        IS one ganglion's optical inference per species),
#                      [[architecture-at-x-is-mathematical-value]]
#                       (@reality/algebra/silicon at value position is
#                        the species ref; admissible at value positions),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (silicon_crystal carrier
#                        + matter_carrier/information_carrier type
#                        aliases per gauge-collapse),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the silicon altitude was implicit in every prior
#                        @epistemologic/reality/silicon/* carrier; this
#                        shard lifts the property altitude to family-root
#                        species altitude),
#                      [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] (no per-pair @glue
#                        /<X>_silicon shards this tick; species admission
#                        lands the contract; per-pair shards follow when
#                        consumers pull — @glue/math_silicon is next).
# Related shards: reality.mirror (the family-root this species'
#                  altitude orbits register at via observe + fold_back;
#                  §3.2.1 forward-promise this shard closes),
#                 reality/algebra.mirror (the species-root this shard
#                  inherits from via `<= @reality/algebra`; the
#                  species_descriptor carrier this shard discharges),
#                 reality/algebra/math.mirror (the parallel math species
#                  at `8bc54412`; the highest-reflexive sibling this
#                  species composes against via @glue/math_silicon),
#                 epistemologic/reality/silicon.mirror (the property
#                  altitude this species lifts; arch, memory,
#                  compute_bound, flake_ref carriers this species
#                  crystallizes over as prior-art),
#                 glue.mirror (the morphism-category discipline the
#                  five per-pair @glue/<X>_silicon species inherit
#                  from; @glue.translate IS the action silicon composes
#                  with math, nl, code, physics, spectral through),
#                 fate.mirror (the constrained-inference operator
#                  selecting which silicon-altitude routine to apply
#                  per tick over the existing Bauchladen of silicon
#                  crystals),
#                 bauchladen.mirror (the content-addressing discipline
#                  silicon crystals respect; each Fortran routine,
#                  LAPACK invocation, kernel-call shape, ISA signature,
#                  memory topology, compute budget, flake reference
#                  lands as a content-addressed crystal),
#                 autopoietic.mirror (the fold-back permission this
#                  species inherits transitively via
#                  @reality/algebra ← @reality ← @autopoietic; each
#                  empirical discharge folds back into the silicon
#                  Bauchladen).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/reality/algebra/silicon.mirror` declares
# `@reality/algebra/silicon` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/cs/turing-1936
source @arxiv/cs/von-neumann-1945
source @arxiv/math/dongarra-demmel-1992
source @arxiv/math/moler-1979
source @arxiv/cs/frigo-leiserson-prokop-ramachandran-1999
source @arxiv/cs/williams-waterman-patterson-2009

prism @reality/algebra/silicon <= @reality/algebra {
  # Silicon-altitude species under @reality. The matter and information
  # carriers below are nominal labels on the same H_silicon state per
  # gauge-collapse (`reality.md` §2.3, path-c uniformity).
  #
  # matter_carrier:      the hardware substrate as typed structure
  #                      (transistor states; ISA + microarch signature;
  #                      memory topology; compute budget; flake
  #                      reference; running-machine configuration).
  # information_carrier: the executable algebra the hardware realizes
  #                      (LAPACK routines; kernel invocations; opcodes;
  #                      LLVM IR; Fortran-compiled binaries; the
  #                      numerical semantics the transistor states
  #                      compute).
  #
  # Under gauge-collapse, these are the same H_silicon state with two
  # nominal projection directions. Per `reality.md` §3.2.1 the silicon
  # species is the altitude at which the substrate's algebra reads as
  # hardware-embodied executable operations.
  type matter_carrier      = H_silicon
  type information_carrier = H_silicon

  # The four invariances of `reality.md` §2.5, discharged at silicon
  # altitude per §3.2.1 items 1-4.
  witness algebra_closure     <- closure_under_5op_at_silicon
  witness hilbert_linearity   <- linearity_under_5op_at_silicon
  witness dirac_equivariance  <- equivariance_under_kintsugi_at_silicon
  witness spectral_invariance <- action_invariance_under_glue_at_silicon

  # The 5-op gauge action at silicon altitude
  focus silicon
  project silicon
  split silicon
  shift silicon
  settle silicon
}

# === The silicon_crystal carrier ===
#
# A typed record per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming one content-
# addressed crystal at the silicon altitude. Per the crystal-kinds
# enumeration above (Fortran routines, LAPACK invocations, kernel-call
# shapes, ISA signatures, memory topologies, compute budgets, flake
# references), the crystal carrier is uniform across kinds — the kind
# ref discriminates.
#
# - `kind`                  the typed ref naming the silicon kind
#                           (e.g., `@arxiv/cs/lapack_routine`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/kernel_call`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/isa_signature`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/memory_topology`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/compute_budget`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/flake_reference`,
#                           `@arxiv/cs/fortran_binary`).
# - `matter_projection`     the matter-aspect projection at silicon
#                           altitude — the hardware substrate's typed
#                           structure (the compiled-binary bytes for
#                           a Fortran routine; the ISA-family tuple
#                           for a signature; the transistor-state
#                           configuration for a running kernel).
# - `information_projection` the information-aspect projection at
#                           silicon altitude — the executable algebra
#                           the hardware realizes (the numerical
#                           semantics for a LAPACK routine; the SIMD-
#                           dispatch policy for an ISA signature; the
#                           UMA-aware codegen policy for a memory
#                           topology). By gauge-collapse, the same
#                           H_silicon state as matter_projection,
#                           differently labeled.
# - `instance_id`           the uuid_spectral identity carrier for
#                           the silicon crystal; the navigable
#                           identity downstream @fate consultations
#                           reference.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (kind, matter_projection,
# information_projection). Two silicon_crystal records ARE the same
# crystal under content-addressing iff all three are byte-equal.
# instance_id is the navigable identity, not the content identity.
type silicon_crystal = {
  kind:                   ref,
  matter_projection:      ref,
  information_projection: ref,
  instance_id:            uuid_spectral,
}

# === crystallize — register a silicon object as a content-addressed
#     crystal in the silicon Bauchladen ===
#
# Given a kind ref + a matter-aspect projection + an information-
# aspect projection, returns the silicon_crystal for the registration.
# The crystal's OID becomes its stable identity; future @fate
# consultations at silicon altitude (or at silicon↔X via @glue) load
# the crystal as prior-art input.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary. Same shape as
# @reality.observe + @reality/algebra/math.crystallize at the
# species-specific altitude (silicon).
crystallize(kind: ref, matter: ref, information: ref) -> silicon_crystal { \ }

# === discharge — emit a silicon_crystal across @io to a hardware-
#     facing surface ===
#
# Silicon crystals discharge to @io through hardware-facing surfaces
# (cargo subprocess, LLVM IR lowering, LAPACK column-major FFI,
# dynamic-library link, Nix flake reference, ...). Given a
# silicon_crystal + a discharge-surface ref, applies the species'
# typed projection to render the crystal to the surface; returns the
# discharge outcome wrapped in @glass's imperfect carrier (residual
# opacity surfaced via transparency<discharge>).
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the realisation MUST
# honor the silicon_discharge_well_typed predicate (the discharge
# surface must be one of the enumerated targets; the rendered output
# must be a valid OID at the @io species' altitude).
discharge(c: silicon_crystal, surface: ref) -> imperfect<ref, ref, transparency(ref)>
requires silicon_discharge_well_typed(c, surface)
{ \ }

# === The bilateral requires obligations ===
#
# Downstream consumers declare bilateral agreement (per recognition
# #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) with the silicon
# species discipline by writing the obligations below.

# The silicon species' @io discharge MUST target one of the enumerated
# hardware-facing surfaces (cargo subprocess, LLVM IR, LAPACK FFI,
# dylib link, flake reference, ...). The species shard does NOT commit
# to ONE surface; the enumeration is open; @fate selects which surface
# per emission. Inheritor consumers discharge by verifying the surface
# ref is in the species' enumerated discharge_target set AND the
# silicon_crystal's kind is admissible for the surface.
silicon_discharge_well_typed(c: silicon_crystal, surface: ref) -> verdict { \ }

# The silicon species' hardware-realization discipline: the crystal's
# information_projection MUST encode content the substrate's 5-op
# algebra can dispatch onto H_silicon (i.e., the crystal IS expressible
# as an executable operation A → End(H_silicon) at the silicon
# altitude's spectral triple). This is the NON-reflexive counterpart
# to `@reality/algebra/math.reflexive_a_side` — silicon carries A as
# gauge that acts UPON silicon-altitude carriers, not as content.
hardware_realized(c: silicon_crystal) -> verdict { \ }

# === The silicon_species_witnessing inheritance predicate ===
#
# `silicon_species_witnessing(c)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral commitment that
# the silicon_crystal `c` IS a valid silicon-altitude crystal under
# the @reality family-root's discipline — i.e., the crystal satisfies
# both obligations above conjointly: silicon_discharge_well_typed
# (on its admissible discharge surface) + hardware_realized.
#
# Sibling to:
#   - `reality.reality_witnessing(o)` (the gauge-orbit inheritance
#     predicate this species' crystals discharge transitively
#     through the species_descriptor's witness_predicate).
#   - `reality/algebra.species_witnessing(s)` (the species-root
#     inheritance predicate this shard's species_descriptor honors).
#   - `reality/algebra/math.math_species_witnessing(c)` (the parallel
#     inheritance predicate at the math species; math↔silicon
#     composition via @glue/math_silicon requires both witnessings
#     conjointly).
#   - `glue.glue_witnessing(c)` (the morphism-correspondence
#     inheritance predicate the five forward-promised
#     @glue/<X>_silicon species discharge per pair).
#
# Forward-promised inheritors (the five @glue/<X>_silicon species land
# as their own shards when consumers pull):
#
#   - `@glue/math_silicon` (math ↔ silicon; LAPACK case; Cholesky
#     first empirical crystal; #74 Standard Model spectral action via
#     Chamseddine-Connes).
#   - `@glue/nl_silicon` (nl ↔ silicon; shell + config lang territory).
#   - `@glue/code_silicon` (code ↔ silicon; compilation boundary).
#   - `@glue/physics_silicon` (physics ↔ silicon; numerical simulation
#     of field configurations).
#   - `@glue/spectral_silicon` (spectral ↔ silicon; substrate-on-
#     substrate at hardware altitude).
#
# No `requires silicon_species_witnessing(...)` clauses at THIS shard.
# The species declares the predicate; consumers add the clauses when
# they pull.
silicon_species_witnessing(c: silicon_crystal) -> verdict { \ }

out @reality/algebra/silicon
out silicon_crystal
out crystallize
out discharge
out silicon_discharge_well_typed
out hardware_realized
out silicon_species_witnessing
